  "body": "Stacked on #2993. Review [the delta above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/fa31e7120ca8c1fdbeceaeec755884b87bb03644...7e3df82930c1275dae6f8108055ca42900bece99).\n\n## What changed\n\nThis head merges #2993 (`fa31e7120`) into the PR branch. Main's rewrite of #2984 (`ee0dafe23`) replaced the old script writer (`crates/post/src/agie/jescript.rs`). Each conflict takes the frame side. Above the merge, one commit adds what main does not have yet:\n\n- A group that mixes `AGIE_QN2` and `AGIE_BERCO_RA035` gets its own refusal, in either work order: `The works of a group must use the same wire condition. This group mixes AGIE_BERCO_RA035 and AGIE_QN2`. The check is in `crates/app/src/posting_agie.rs`, before the single-punch limit of CCB035. No job directory is written. Before this change, the frame refused the same group with the single-punch text, which did not name the mixed conditions. A group that requests `AGIE_BERCO_RA035` for every work still gets the single-punch text.\n- The machine template `agiecut-classic-2s.mch` no longer tells the user to set X/Y travel endpoints. The native wire EDM post refuses a profile that states them.\n- The decision file `docs/decisions/2984-agie-quality-binding.md`, with a section that lists what main already covers.\n\n## What main already covers (dropped from this PR)\n\nEach item was checked on `fa31e7120`:\n\n- Zero working steps on import: `crates/post/src/agie_setup/piece.rs` writes one quality object for the piece and `ASDELETE` for each work. No `ASAGIE` (asserted in `crates/post/src/agie/tests.rs`, `group_tests.rs`, `quality_tests.rs`). The receipt reports `working_steps_generated: false` (`crates/app/src/script/report.rs:83`). From `ee0dafe23` and the stack ports.\n- One requested quality for each piece, CCB030 or CCB035, with the receipt offsets and the user-guide TECCUT procedure (#2966 port, `agie_setup/quality.rs`, `docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md`).\n- The repeat-import \"new piece\" text (user guide, line 164) and the refusal of a stated X or Y travel (`crates/app/src/posting_agie.rs`, test `generic_preview_inside_declared_travel_cannot_clear_native_offsets`).\n- The smoothing skip of the native post (`crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs`, `posting::agie::is_native`), the plasma-stream refusal (`crates/app/tests/plasma_post_refusals.rs`) and the 11 recorded-stream refusal goldens (`crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/agie-native/*.refusal`). The frame text is \"Native wire EDM job files require ...\". The PR text was \"Agie native wire EDM requires ...\".\n- The default-machine diagnostic (#3092, on main).\n\n## Readings\n\n- `a_group_with_mixed_wire_conditions_is_refused_in_either_order`: both orders exit non-zero with the exact text above, and `PAIR20` does not exist.\n- No posted byte changes. The diff against `fa31e7120` touches no golden and no writer.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-app --test agie_native`: `quality::a_group_with_mixed_wire_conditions_is_refused_in_either_order` (new), and the existing `quality::ra035_refuses_a_group_an_arc_punch_a_die_and_a_cutoff`, `quality::the_saved_condition_selects_the_exact_requested_quality`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No control import for this head. No job bytes change, so the control results of #2993 stay valid.\n- No physical cut.\n- No heavy step. The issue is `P6`.\n\n## Gate\n\n`CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on `7e3df8293`: 1201 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 46.9 min. The plan included `post suites: script_agie_native` and `app suites: agie_native`. It also included `clippy -D warnings` with `--all-targets` on geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, app, gpu and ui.\n\n`git merge-tree --write-tree 7e3df8293 origin/main` is clean.\n\nChangelog: A native wire EDM group that mixes the AGIE_QN2 and AGIE_BERCO_RA035 conditions is refused with a message that names the two conditions.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nAgainst current main, this PR adds two recorded programs. Both come from the parent #2993 (tangent-loop writer, `crates/post/src/agie/tangent_profile.rs`, export through `export_round_with_review`), which is in this PR's diff until #2993 merges. This PR's own delta above #2993 adds or changes no recorded program. No golden that is on main changes.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/agie-native/ROUND20.ISO` (A): the `examples/agie/rounded-punch.camscript` job. A convex punch from one selected DXF chain of four straight lines and four tangent corner arcs (two arcs of radius 6 mm, two of radius 4 mm; centres (14,−8), (16,10), (−14,8), (−16,−10)), on 20 mm stock, quality CCB030. Nominal geometry with incremental I/J arc centres, counter-clockwise, entry from the waste side on a straight side, 1 mm separation.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/agie-native/THREEARC.ISO` (A): the `examples/agie/three-corner-punch.camscript` job. A convex punch from three tangent arcs (centres (24,0), (0,18), (0,0)) joined by straight sides, one of them oblique, on 20 mm stock, quality CCB030. Same rules as ROUND20.\n\nBoth programs were imported on the emulated control on 24 Nov 2026 (`agie-imports-20261125/ROUND20` and `THREEARC`): zero steps at import, the 20 mm TECCUT row, `CCB030[4]` after TECCUT, `geen fouten`, every arc centre kept on every pass, 1.000 mm separation. The files are byte-identical at this head.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #2984\n\n",
